# Application Features Analysis

## Overview
The **MicroLearning Bot** is a comprehensive educational platform combining a Telegram Bot interface for learners and a Web Dashboard for administrators. It utilizes AI Agents (Google Gemini via Agno) for dynamic content delivery, assessment, and documentation support.

## 1. Telegram Bot (Learner Interface)
The primary interface for users to interact with learning content.

### Core Learning Features
-   **Daily Video Delivery** (`/video`):
    -   Delivers microlearning videos based on user progress.
    -   Tracks watch history and completion status.
    -   Supports progressive difficulty levels.
-   **Interactive Quizzes** (`/quiz`):
    -   Generates conceptual questions based on the last watched video.
    -   **AI Evaluation**: Uses AI to rate user answers (0-10) and provide qualitative feedback.
    -   Supports open-ended questions testing deep understanding.
-   **Progress Tracking** (`/progress`):
    -   Displays statistics on watched videos and completion rates.
    -   Shows quiz performance (average score, total questions answered).

### RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation) Support
-   **Document Querying** (`/ask`):
    -   Allows users to ask natural language questions about company documents (SOPs, manuals).
    -   Uses vector search (ChromaDB) to find relevant context.
    -   Generates accurate, cited answers using LLM.
-   **Document Listing** (`/docs`):
    -   Lists available resources accessible to the user.

## 2. Admin Dashboard (Web Interface)
A Flask-based web application for managing the platform.

### Dashboard & Analytics
-   **Overview Stats**: Real-time metrics on total users, active videos, quiz attempts, and engagement.
-   **Activity Monitoring**: Tracks daily and weekly active users.
-   **Visualizations**: Charts for user growth and engagement (implied by templates).

### User Management
-   **CRUD Operations**: Add, Edit, Delete, and Toggle status of users.
-   **Department Grouping**: Organizes users by roles (HR, Sales, IT).
-   **Individual Progress**: specific view for each user's video history and quiz scores.

### Content Management
-   **Video Management**:
    -   Upload and manage video content.
    -   **Video Creation Tool**: Built-in editor to upload clips, arrange them, and compile into a single video with transitions and title screens.
    -   Categorization (Onboarding, Technical, Business).
-   **Question Management**:
    -   Manual creation of questions linked to videos.
    -   Specify difficulty, concepts tested, and question type.
    -   View and manage questions per video.

## 3. Intelligent Agents (Backend)
The system is powered by an **Agent Orchestrator** that routes requests to specialized agents.

-   **Video Agent**: Manages video logic, file handling (Local/URL/Telegram ID), and delivery tracking.
-   **Question Agent**:
    -   **Dynamic Generation**: Can generate questions from video transcripts or *direct video analysis* (using Gemini 1.5 Pro).
    -   **Assessment**: Evaluates free-text answers against key concepts.
-   **RAG Agent**: Handles document embedding, retrieval, and synthesis of answers.

## 4. Technical Features
-   **Database**: SQLite with SQLAlchemy ORM (User, Video, Question, QuizAttempt, Document models).
-   **Video Processing**: Capabilities to stitch clips, add transitions, and generate thumbnails ([utils/video_processor.py](file:///c:/Users/bmith/OneDrive/Desktop/projects%20-2025/MicroLearning/Agents/utils/video_processor.py)).
-   **Scalability**: Designed with Agno (AgentOS) principles for independent agent operation.
